Native Oolite-like loader:
- Exposed a game/global script host function expandDescription() (controlled
  resource lookup fixture only, not the complete original ResourceManager)
- Bound real global self (this.global=this)
- Created the canonical immutable OOJSWorldScripts registry and a real
  OOGFOSScriptObjects per-script instance. Registered world script name
  'oolite-locale-functions', using the same JSValue object identity.
- Loaded the ENTIRE UNMODIFIED original locale script in per-script this
  context. The original script registered formatInteger and formatCredits
  on the shared Oolite global scope.
- Validated number grouping, deci-credit formatting, credit rounding and
  world script identity, returning 42.

Real bug corrected: JS_ToString returns a SIGNED STRING LENGTH, not JSERR_*.
First guest run failed because the fixture incorrectly tested !=JSERR_OK.
After changing to <0 for conversion failure, original script loaded and
passed RC 0. That distinction should be respected in other GFOS adapters.

Limitations: expandDescription is a fixture returning pinned lookup examples;
not the real Oolite ResourceManager. Entire script runs native but original
game/UI/cockpit/flight not yet executed without legacy SpiderMonkey.
